{
  "title": { "en": "The generator meets “any”" },
  "adds": ["anyR", "swapConcl", "consFront", "mkRule", "eachOf", "keepBound"],
  "tray": "machine",
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "The board holds your <part-ref to=\"lemma:elimGen\"></part-ref> as it is now. The intro rule of <level-ref to=\"decl-ex\"></level-ref>, ⋀x. ⟦?P(x)⟧ ⟹ ∃y. ?P(y), first takes any thing x: in the generator it is a rule binding x, not a plain rule, and Swap conclusion does not accept it."
      }
    },
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "The new part Keep ⋀ is a frame: when a rule begins with bound variables, the frame works on the rule after them and puts the same bound variables back in front of its output; when there are none, the frame works on the input itself."
      }
    }
  ],
  "after": {
    "en": "This is why <part-ref to=\"part:exE\"></part-ref> gives that thing a new name."
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "gen-ex",
      "kind": "machine",
      "want": "elim",
      "inputs": [
        { "name": "it", "label": { "en": "It" } },
        { "name": "ways", "label": { "en": "Intro rules (a list)" } }
      ],
      "tests": [
        { "it": "?A ∧ ?B", "ways": ["⟦?A; ?B⟧ ⟹ ?A ∧ ?B"], "elim": ["?A ∧ ?B", "⟦?A; ?B⟧ ⟹ ?R"] },
        { "it": "?A ∨ ?B", "ways": ["⟦?A⟧ ⟹ ?A ∨ ?B", "⟦?B⟧ ⟹ ?A ∨ ?B"], "elim": ["?A ∨ ?B", "⟦?A⟧ ⟹ ?R", "⟦?B⟧ ⟹ ?R"] },
        { "it": "⊥", "ways": [], "elim": ["⊥"] },
        { "it": "?A ↔ ?B", "ways": ["⟦?A → ?B; ?B → ?A⟧ ⟹ ?A ↔ ?B"], "elim": ["?A ↔ ?B", "⟦?A → ?B; ?B → ?A⟧ ⟹ ?R"] },
        { "it": "∃y. ?P(y)", "ways": ["⋀x. ⟦?P(x)⟧ ⟹ ∃y. ?P(y)"], "elim": ["∃y. ?P(y)", "⋀x. ⟦?P(x)⟧ ⟹ ?R"] }
      ],
      "hidden": [
        {
          "it": "∃u. ∃v. ?P(u, v)",
          "ways": ["⋀x y. ⟦?P(x, y)⟧ ⟹ ∃u. ∃v. ?P(u, v)"],
          "elim": ["∃u. ∃v. ?P(u, v)", "⋀x y. ⟦?P(x, y)⟧ ⟹ ?R"]
        }
      ],
      "brief": {
        "en": "Upgrade the elimination rule generator so that it also works when an intro rule has bound variables."
      },
      "hint": [
        {
          "en": "Compare the intro rule of “there is” with the case to make: which part stays the same?"
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "r = anyR()",
        "e = eachOf(ways, body: a) {",
        "  body {",
        "    a = keepBound(e.body, body: s) {",
        "      body {",
        "        s = swapConcl(a.body, r)",
        "      }",
        "    }",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "c = consFront(it, e)",
        "m = mkRule(c, r)",
        "out <- m"
      ],
      "naive": [
        "r = anyR()",
        "e = eachOf(ways, body: s) {",
        "  body {",
        "    s = swapConcl(e.body, r)",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "c = consFront(it, e)",
        "m = mkRule(c, r)",
        "out <- m"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
